EERRRROORRSS
     The ssoouurrcceeffiilltteerr functions may fail because of:

     [EADDRNOTAVAIL]    The network interface which the interface argument
                        refers to was not configured in the system, or the
                        system is not a member of the group.

     [EAFNOSUPPORT]     The group and/or one or more of the slist arguments
                        were of an address family unsupported by the system,
                        or the address family of the group and slist arguments
                        were not identical.

     [EINVAL]           The group argument does not contain a multicast ad‐
                        dress.  The fmode argument is invalid; it must be set
                        to either MCAST_INCLUDE or MCAST_EXCLUDE.  The numsrc
                        or slist arguments do not specify a source list.

     [ENOMEM]           Insufficient memory was available to carry out the re‐
                        quested operation.

